10
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,380
I start my new job in two weeks.

11
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:54,300
My human resources manager wants to conduct an interview with me before I leave.

12
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,440
Ah, an exit interview.

13
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,220
Are you looking forward to it?

14
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,380
I'm not sure how I feel about it.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,700
I resigned because I've been unhappy at that company for a time.

16
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:08,140
But I'm not sure if I should tell them how I really feel.

17
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:13,220
To my way of thinking, there are two main potential benefits that come from

18
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:17,140
unleashing an agitated stream of truth during an exit interview.

19
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:19,540
The first is release.

20
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:25,080
Unburdening yourself of frustration and perhaps even anger to someone who isn't a

21
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:28,500
friend or close colleague can be wonderfully freeing.

22
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:34,060
And let me guess, the second is that the criticism will, theoretically, help the

23
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:35,960
organisation I'm leaving to improve?

24
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:40,860
Making sure employees of the future are less likely to encounter what I did?

25
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:46,160
That's right. But the problem with the company improvement part is that very often

26
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,060
it doesn't happen.

27
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:51,420
An exit interview is supposed to be private, but often isn't.

28
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:56,360
In my company, the information gained from these interviews is often not

29
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:02,020
confidential and the information is used as dirt against another manager or can be

30
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:03,660
traded among senior managers.

31
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,060
Now you've got me rethinking what I'll disclose in the interview.

32
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:12,880
There is always the chance that it could affect my reputation and my ability to

33
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,000
network in the industry.

34
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,200
It is a pretty small industry after all.

35
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:22,780
you initially gain from the instant satisfaction of telling it like it is, you might

36
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:26,220
lose down the track by injuring your future career prospects.

37
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:31,740
Right. Perhaps I would be better getting things off my chest by going to one of

38
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:33,800
those Rate Your Employer websites.

39
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,980
You could. And don't do the interview at all.

40
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,540
Exit interviews are not mandatory.

