Conversation 2. Today I'm talking to the renowned botanist Jane Forster.

45
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:10,240
Thank you for inviting me to join you on the show, Henry.

46
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:16,040
Recently, Jane, you've become quite a celebrity since the release of your latest

47
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:19,300
documentary. Can you tell us a little about it?

48
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:25,160
Well, it follows my expedition to study the vegetation indigenous to the rainforest

49
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,080
in equatorial areas of Southeast Asia.

50
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:32,740
You certainly get to travel to some very exotic locations.

51
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:35,700
It was far from glamorous, to be honest.

52
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:41,380
The area we visited was accessible only by canoe, and the living conditions in the

53
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:43,900
hut were primitive, to say the least.

54
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:48,520
There was no electricity, and our water supply was a nearby stream.

55
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:51,600
How were the weather conditions while you were there?

56
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:56,980
The weather was not conducive to our work at all, since the humidity was almost

57
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:00,660
unbearable. At midday, we stayed in the hut and did nothing.

58
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:04,020
It was too humid to either work or sleep.

59
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:06,400
How long did your team spend in the jungle?

60
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,720
Originally, we planned to be there for a month, but in the end, we stayed for only

61
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:15,100
two weeks. Why did you cut the expedition short?

62
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:20,580
Halfway through the trip, we received news that a hurricane was approaching, and we

63
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:22,800
had to evacuate at very short notice.

64
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,740
That sounds like a fascinating anecdote.

65
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:27,280
It was frightening.

66
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,360
The fastest evacuation route was through river rapids.

67
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,880
We had to navigate them carrying all of our equipment.

68
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:38,240
So overall, was the journey unsuccessful?

69
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:43,560
Absolutely not. We gathered a massive amount of data about the local plant life.

70
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:47,060
Why do you put up with such adverse conditions?

71
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:50,520
Botany is an obsession for me.

72
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:55,460
Many of the destinations I visit have stunning scenery, and I get to meet a variety

73
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:57,440
of people from all over the world.

74
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:00,460
So where will your next destination be?

75
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,380
I haven't decided yet.

76
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,220
Then we can leave it for another occasion.

77
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:36,240
Thanks! Question 6 Why does the woman describe her experience as far from glamorous?

