87
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:08,200
with laymen. Most of them don't realise the harmful effects of this practice.

88
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:13,740
In a new study, people exposed to jargon when reading about subjects like autonomous

89
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:19,200
vehicles and surgical robots later said they were less interested in science than

90
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:24,120
others who read about the same topics but without the use of specialised terms.

91
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:30,760
They also felt less informed about science and less qualified to discuss science

92
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:37,000
topics. It's noteworthy that it made no difference if the jargon terms were defined

93
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:37,700
in the text.

94
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:44,020
Even when the terms were defined, readers still felt the same lack of engagement as

95
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:47,220
readers who read jargon that wasn't explained.

96
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:54,280
The problem is that the mere presence of jargon sends a discouraging message to

97
00:08:54,280 --> 00:09:00,580
readers. Hilary Schulman, the author of the study, asserts that specialised words

98
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,880
are a signal.

99
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:06,500
Jargon tells people that the message isn't for them.

100
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:11,220
There's an even darker side to how people react to jargon.

101
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:16,980
In another study, researchers found that reading scientific articles containing

102
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:20,980
jargon led people to doubt the actual science.

103
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:26,360
They found the opposite when a text is easier to read.

104
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,440
Then, people are more persuaded.

105
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:36,180
Thus, it's important to communicate clearly when talking about complex science

106
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:42,640
subjects. This is especially true with issues related to public health, like the

107
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:47,160
safety of new medications and the benefits of vaccines.

108
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:53,960
Schulman concedes that the use of jargon is appropriate with scientific audiences.

109
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:59,680
But, scientists who want to communicate with the general public need to modify their

110
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:02,760
language. They need to eliminate jargon.

