198
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:33,220
Iron ore is a key ingredient in steelmaking.

199
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:39,700
The mining companies here produce almost 300 million tons of iron ore a year.

200
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:46,920
The 240 giant autonomous trucks in use in the Western Australian mines can weigh 400

201
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:52,180
tons fully loaded and travel at speeds of up to 60 kilometers per hour.

202
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:58,120
They are a technological leap, transporting iron ore along routes which run for

203
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:01,660
hundreds of kilometers from mines to their destinations.

204
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:07,140
Here, when the truck arrives at its destination, staff in the operations center

205
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:09,500
direct it precisely where to unload.

206
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:15,860
Vast quantities of iron ore are then transported by autonomous trains to ocean

207
00:20:15,860 --> 00:20:21,300
ports. Advocates argue these automated vehicles will change mining forever.

208
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:27,500
It may only be five years before the use of automation technology leads to a fully

209
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:34,280
robotic mine. A range of factors has pushed Western Australia's desert region to the

210
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:36,260
lead of this automation revolution.

211
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:42,280
These include the huge size of the mines, the scale of equipment, and the repetitive

212
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,840
nature of some of the work.

213
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,640
Then there's the area's remoteness.

214
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:53,160
At 502,000 square kilometers, it can sometimes make recruiting staff a challenge.

215
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:57,940
Another consideration is the risks when humans interact with large machinery.

216
00:20:58,260 --> 00:21:01,160
There are also the financial imperatives.

217
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:06,520
The ongoing push by the mining corporations to be more productive and more efficient

218
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:10,760
is another powerful driver in embracing automation technology.

219
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:16,460
The concept of a autonomous mine is a bit of a misleading term, however.

220
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:21,100
This is because the more technology is put into the field, the more people are

221
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:24,400
needed to deploy, maintain, and improve it.

222
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:29,820
The automation and digitization of the industry is creating a need for different

223
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:35,620
jobs. These include data scientists and engineers in automation and artificial

224
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:41,260
intelligence. The mining companies claim automation and robotics present

225
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:45,080
opportunities to make mining more sustainable and safer.

226
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:50,700
Employees will be offered a career that is even more fulfilling and more rewarding.

227
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:57,720
Workers' have accepted the inevitability of the introduction of new technology, but

228
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:01,340
they still have reservations about the rise of automation technology.

229
00:22:01,340 --> 00:22:06,160
Their main concern is the potential impact on remote communities.

230
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:12,200
As automation spreads further, the question is how these remote communities will

231
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:14,900
survive when the old jobs are eliminated.

232
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:21,100
And this may well prove to be the most significant impact of robotic technology in

233
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:22,820
many places around the world.

